From 8ddaf07e65859fae118544bdf0c41421bfbc441c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 22:41:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [feature](be) Refactor native stack collector to ck-style
 signal handler

Rewrite be/src/service/http/action/native_stack_action.cpp so its signal
handling mirrors <ck>/src/Storages/System/StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp.
The previous freeform implementation passed a per-thread slot pointer
through sival_ptr and polled a per-slot atomic with sleep; this version
uses ClickHouse's pattern instead:

- A single sequence number is stored in siginfo_t.si_value.sival_int and
  is incremented after each thread.
- A single global capture buffer holds the frames; one thread is
  signalled at a time and the buffer is serialized by the dump mutex.
- A pipe(2) is used as the data-ready notification channel; the HTTP
  handler polls it with the configured timeout.
- The handler enforces the anti-spoof check (si_pid == server_pid) and
  the signal_latch compare-exchange.
- A per-thread is_signal_blocked check skips threads that block SIGRTMIN
  so the wait does not have to time out for nothing.
- rt_tgsigqueueinfo is still used as the primary send path; tgkill is
  kept as a best-effort fallback (loses the sequence-num passthrough,
  so the handler ignores tgkill-delivered signals).

Doris environment deviations from ck (each documented inline):
- pipe2(O_CLOEXEC) replaces ck's LazyPipeFDs (internal type).
- No DENY_ALLOCATIONS_IN_SCOPE; the no-alloc/no-lock/no-log invariant
  is enforced by inspection and a header comment in the handler.
- libunwind replaces ck's StackTrace class.

Every refactored function carries a // Reference:
<ck>/src/Storages/System/StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp:N comment.

Reference: <ck>/src/Storages/System/StorageSystemStackTrace.cpp:71-758
